/* The game's palette and the defaults every screen shares. `global.cosmos` is the global layer
   of the cascade: its selectors reach into every component, and the variables here are visible
   to the other stylesheets in this folder (menus.cosmos, hud.cosmos).

   Sizes are window points: 1px is one pixel on a normal display and two on a Retina one.
   Lantern draws text with its 8x8 bitmap font, so a font-size picks the nearest whole multiple
   of 8: 16px is the font's normal size, 24px is 1.5x that, and so on. */
:root {
    --accent: #FFD24D;
    --accent-light: #FFE89A;
    --ink: #141420;
    --text: #EBEBF2;
    --muted: #8F98B3;
    --panel-top: #1B2440E6;
    --panel-bottom: #0B1022E6;
    --line: #FFFFFF26;
}

text {
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: 16px;
}

/* The root GameUi:::Mount puts on screen: the whole window, so the screens inside can place
   themselves against it. */
.game-screen {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0px;
    left: 0px;
    width: 100vw;
    height: 100vh;
}
